WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.630
Someone once said...

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:06.630
There are kites with wings of 
soft, smooth udon noodles...

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.300
Udon Kites!

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:18.150
There is paprika that tastes like sweet 
pudding and melts in your mouth...

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.620
Papuddingka!

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.150
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.260
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.060
Ichiryu, the president of IGO,

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:40.500
gave Toriko a list of seven 
training ingredients to capture.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.970
Ozone Grass, which grows 
in the Vegetable Sky...

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.610
The legendary Melk's Stardust, 
found in Heavy Hole...

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.840
Mellow Cola, found in the Gourmet Pyramid...

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.650
There are four left!

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.020
Toriko's journey to capture 
training ingredients continues!

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.720
Glittering Crystal! Shining Gourami!

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.760
Jeez... He calls me here, 
then leaves me hanging...

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.170
Toriko-san sure is late...

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.400
Mmm... Ham Fish on top 
of Tsuchinoko Shrimp...

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.240
What a delicious combination!

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.850
I think I'm going to cry!

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.780
You're not even listening to me...

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.650
The midsummer sea breeze imbues the 
Ham Fish with an even saltier flavor.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.190
It's light, but goes wonderfully with 
the plump, succulent Tsuchinoko Shrimp.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:45.160
It's harmony, right? A harmony of tastes.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.530
Matsu, harmony isn't taste 
alone, though, is it?

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.540
Ponkochi, would you turn 
up the volume a little?

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:57.410
Oh, yeah, got it. But how about 
switching to a whole new plate?

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.540
Right now, some lively samba is playing,

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:02.180
but listen up, I'm getting 
ready with bossa nova.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.680
That's great, Ponkochi! You're the best!

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:08.950
Sunny-san...

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.620
Who is that man?

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.960
A freelance Gourmet Planner, Ponkochi.

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:19.200
Every dish has music that 
perfectly matches the taste.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:23.700
He's a Gourmet DJ that provides 
just the right sound for each dish.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.840
Gourmet DJ?

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:29.910
A professional who brings forth a beautiful 
session between food and music.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:33.010
It costs a ton to hire 
him, two million an hour,

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:36.510
but he's totally booked up 
for the next several months.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.180
Two million an hour?!

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.020
Yes. Harmony through and through!

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.820
Do you understand, Matsu?

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.730
You can't just have harmony with taste alone!

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.860
The restaurant's interior, the tableware,

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.100
the temperature, humidity, and 
yes, the background music!

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:01.570
When everything is in harmony, then 
you can call it a perfect meal!

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:04.540
But...

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.680
The average person can't afford to pay 
that much money for music during a meal.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.710
Stupid... You! Matsu!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:12.110
Yes?

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.080
You're a chef, so you'd better pay 
careful attention to that, too!

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:16.450
Right...

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:19.050
Good grief...

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.030
So, how was it?

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.400
The Gourmet Pyramid.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:37.300
Oh, right...

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:42.080
First, the Desert Labyrinth 
was an incredible place...

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:47.710
See, the sand, it was like swish, 
it's that quicksand stuff...

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.380
And it did move really quickly...

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.590
It was a harrowing trip 
and we went through a lot,

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:31.020
but thanks to Zebra-san, we got 
the Mellow Cola in the end.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.590
I got to drink delicious cola.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.730
And with Zebra?! Unbelievable!

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:39.530
I mean, you and that lowdown 
scoundrel? It's unfathomable!

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:43.500
Well, he did pick fights 
sometimes with Toriko-san...

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.070
And he was quick to get angry if 
he suspected you of being cocky...

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.110
It was a little tough...

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:51.710
There's no end of hardships on your trips.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.810
Well, I wouldn't say that...

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:56.380
Maybe a few hardships...

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:01.150
Toriko-san really is late...

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.090
Isn't it a hard job

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:08.590
being partners with a selfish, 
vulgar guy like Toriko, honestly?

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.030
Oh, I wouldn't go that...

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.230
It's because he doesn't give 
"harmony" even a passing thought.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.670
And I'm positive he's having a 
negative effect on your own progress!

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.340
You think so?

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:26.910
Listen, Matsu...

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.480
Take this opportunity to become my par...

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.050
I've kept you waiting.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.220
A talking cow!

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:47.430
Hi!

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.230
Toriko-san! You scared the heck out of me!

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.940
Sorry 'bout that!

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.610
You know, you're the one who called us here!

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:59.310
And on the way, I ran into a Ass Cow!

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:00.910
Whoof!

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.750
An ass! An ass-faced cow!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.080
Hey, would you prepare this for me?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:08.680
Um...

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:09.950
You want some, Sunny?

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.550
No, absolutely not.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.690
Is that Tsuchinoko Shrimp?!

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:18.860
Get me some of that, too!

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.700
And Thunder Beer!

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.330
Y-Yes, sir! Right away!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.300
What's up, Ponkochi?!

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.470
Yo, yo, been a while, yo, yo, Toriko!

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:31.370
This is the perfect song for 
you! 1, 2, Knife! 5, 6, Fork!

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.470
Sorry, but I came here to talk to Sunny.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.040
Could you turn it off for a while?

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:36.540
Alright?

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:37.710
Yo.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:38.980
Yo...

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:40.450
Yo...

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:47.020
Feels like an electric current's 
runnin' through my body!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.720
Thunder Beer's the best!

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:51.690
Get me another one!

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:52.760
Yes, sir! Right away...

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:55.330
Yo, yo, I got nothin' to do...

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.630
Thank you for the food!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.770
This Ass Cow is delicious!

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.940
Hey, Sunny, you sure you don't want some?

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.710
This is a great piece of Ass Cow!

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.410
No thank you, I said!

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:17.280
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.690
Although I'm sure it concerns a job...

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.590
Just what kind of ingredient this time?

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:26.290
You're right. It's one of the training 
ingredients from Old Man Ichiryu.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:28.460
A training ingredient?!

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.730
Forget it. You do it yourself.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:31.930
Pain in the neck...

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.270
Toriko-san, what is the ingredient?!

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.840
Shining Gourami.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:42.740
Shining Gourami!

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:47.610
A translucent, brilliantly glittering 
fish that's as beautiful as crystal!

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.980
People also call it... Crystal Fish!

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.360
Why are you the only one who gets to 
go after prey as beautiful as that?!

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.120
Hey!

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.660
Hell if I know! Ask the old man!

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.960
Um...

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:05.130
Is the ingredient so hard to get 
that we need Sunny-san's help?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.800
Yeah. The problem is its habitat.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:15.110
It's one of the three great 
falls in the world, Death Falls!

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:20.840
Shining Gourami live in a cavern 
inside that gigantic waterfall.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.520
Death Falls is also called Execution Falls.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.450
A trillion liters of water fall every second.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:32.960
T-Trillion?! That's so overwhelming, 
I can't even imagine it!

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:36.190
I recall hearing that the thickness 
of the waterfall is one kilometer...

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:40.460
Hypothetically, no matter how 
much artillery you fire at it...

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:41.560
Boom.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.030
Boom.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:45.500
It will never get through.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.240
They're called Death Falls

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:50.070
because anything that gets close is 
executed by the water guillotine.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:54.280
That's right.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:11:00.350
Death Falls' gigantic water bombshells 
pulverize everything they touch.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.520
They don't let anyone inside.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.460
It's a gross environment that's 
even on par with the Gourmet World.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.090
In other words, it's a place the 
old man would probably like.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:12.560
What do you think, Sunny?

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:16.900
It's the perfect place to test how far 
you've come in your training, right?

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:24.540
Certainly, I am interested 
in Shining Gourami.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:26.470
Besides...

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:32.380
It may be just the place to 
bathe my new family member,

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:34.780
who came from the Gourmet World.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.530
T-Toriko-san!!

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:50.530
Is that...?!

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:06.980
Don't tell me that's a...

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.480
Mother Snake.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:10.280
Her name is Queen.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:12.920
My new family member. Be nice to her.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.860
You mean, she's your partner, Sunny-san?!

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:21.930
This is the first time 
I've seen a Mother Snake.

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:23.500
Is this still a kid?

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:24.430
Yeah.

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:27.230
A kid this size?!

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:31.070
Mother Snakes are giant snakes that are 
said to be the mothers of all snakes.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:33.540
They're legendary snakes 
that are said to grow

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.010
almost as long as the 
circumference of the planet.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:38.710
The circumference of the planet?!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.810
Just how many meters is that?!

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.280
Do snakes like that really exist?!

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.250
Well, shall we get going then?

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:47.720
To Death Falls...

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.060
Just this once, I'll let 
you have a ride on Queen.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:55.060
Hurry up and hop on!

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:57.100
Sunny! I'll owe you for this!

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:58.430
We're riding on that?

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.300
Wait a second!

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.370
Make sure you take your shoes off!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:11.680
Wow! Its scale!

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:13.710
You can use it as a chair.

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:14.250
Thank you!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.050
Alright, let's go, Queen!

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.620
Amazing!

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:42.270
Super-duper gigantic snake! Baby, bet 
your ass it scared the hell outta me, yo!

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:43.670
What a catch!

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.420
Hold on tight, Matsu!

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.320
It's going too fast!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.850
You're lucky. It's not every day you get 
to ride on the head of a Mother Snake!

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.060
Lucky?!

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.730
They're a rare species that mainly 
dwells in the Gourmet World!

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:05.360
Because of its massive length,

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.500
even the occasional eyewitness sightings

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.200
in the Human World are of the body only.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:15.040
So being able to see the head 
or tail is a sign of good luck!

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:16.370
Right?!

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:20.140
But forget about seeing the 
head, you're actually riding it,

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:21.880
so how lucky is that?!

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:25.980
This is no time to be talking 
about how lucky I am!

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.050
Toriko, that's not quite accurate.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:31.120
Certainly, even amongst the tough 
Beasts of the Gourmet World,

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:34.220
the head of the Mother Snake is rarely seen.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.660
There's a reason for that.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.260
It's not as though the head <i>isn't</i> seen.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:41.330
It's that all those who see the 
head are subsequently eaten.

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:42.260
What?!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:45.530
The Mother Snake is one of the strongest 
Beasts in the Gourmet World.

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:49.670
Queen is still a child, though, 
so it's not <i>that</i> strong...

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:51.570
Beautiful, isn't she?

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:55.110
She would never show her face 
to the great uncool masses.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:59.180
She's overflowing with 
grace, my ultimate beauty!

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:04.650
Sunny-san, we've gotten a good 
look at Queen-chan's face!

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:09.860
Th-That doesn't mean we're going 
to be eaten later on, does it?!

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.960
Don't ask me.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:13.760
I dunno.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:15.660
You dunno?! Hey!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:17.530
Matsu!

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.770
Say if you were to become my partner,

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.440
I'd see to it that you were never eaten.

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:30.840
Nothing!

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.150
Queen, bypass the forest!

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:39.150
It's going too fast!

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:58.700
It just ate something!

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:03.310
They say frogs lose the power to 
move when a snake stares at them,

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:06.980
but when it comes to a Mother Snake, 
there's no staring, only eating!

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.110
This certainly is an incredible speed.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:11.520
400 kilometers an hour, I'd guess.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:16.120
400 kilometers an hour?! That's faster 
than the Gourmet Bullet Train!

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:19.790
The entire body of a snake is a mass 
of muscle, so it can move as it likes.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:23.800
You could say it's like a bullet train 
that's able to alter its course at will!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.400
That's some mighty fine mobility!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:29.000
Queen is still a child. So 
this is as fast as she gets.

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:30.570
As fast as she gets?!

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:35.670
Apparently, an adult Mother Snake 
moves as fast as a shooting star.

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:38.340
Faster than this?!

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:42.050
There are Gourmet Hunters who 
make a wish when they see it.

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:44.280
Like I was sayin', it is a lucky thing!

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:46.280
You may be right.

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:49.190
Maybe super-lucky!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.890
That's the rarely-seen Mirror Lychee!

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:53.890
Queen!

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:06.040
Without thinking, I hustled over here 
to get these beautiful, sparkling,

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:07.440
flushed...

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.250
You can't tell by the way it looks,

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:18.480
but it's got a dazzling sweetness 
that makes you want to dance!

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:20.050
Great! Just great!

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.850
Hey! Give me one!

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.790
Forget it! Pick your own!

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:31.190
That's Baby Beef, that tastes like yakiniku!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.660
Flying Knife!

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.300
Alright!

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:40.540
Hey!

00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:00.160
No way!

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:02.660
Toriko-san!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.600
Please go easy on me.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:11.770
It's Sunny's fault for suddenly 
changing this thing's course.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:16.000
I spotted Collashrooms, which are 
full of skin beautifying collagen!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.410
Can you blame me?!

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:23.880
I don't think I can take any more of this...

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.370
Stop!

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:09.260
We're here.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.260
The Mors Mountains!

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:16.560
With an elevation of over 15,000 meters,

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:19.870
it's the fifth-tallest mountain 
range in the Human World!

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:25.470
The Shining Gourami live at 
the base of this mountain,

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.040
inside Death Falls!

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:26.360
We give thanks for this food, let's eat!

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:32.200
Yuuuu... Toriko!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:34.970
Potassium, manganese, calcium, 
starch, fructose, and dextrose

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:37.770
Magnesium, iron, vitamins ABCDE

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.640
Vanadium, sodium, glucosamine, chondroitin

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.480
Carotintintin, lycopenpenpene, 
isoflavonvonvone

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:46.180
Celery, goya, and green peas

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:49.020
Shiitake, liver, eggplant, bell pepper

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.720
What a shame to say "I don't 
even want to look at them!"

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.390
Even if you hate it, gobble 
it down 3 times or 4 times

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.820
and it'll be more and more

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.160
Yuuuu... Toriko!

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.960
Eat 'em up more! Eat 'em up more!

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:01.830
More and more and more and 
more and more! Eat 'em all up!

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:06.100
Delicious things are delicious!  
Not even giving them a chance…

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:07.400
Such a waste!

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:10.270
Gobble 'em down more! Gobble 'em down more!

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:13.040
Majorly, deeply, plentifully, 
heartily, gobble 'em down!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:18.680
They enrich your body and spirit! 
Be grateful to your meals today!

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:21.580
Thanks for the food! All done!

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.720
This week's Gourmet Fortune!

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:28.820
We're starting a new segment today!

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:31.690
It's time for Gourmet Fortune, with 
a heaping helping of accuracy!

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:36.300
We're going to use a camera 
later, so get yours ready!

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:39.800
Now then, choose one of these three platters.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.640
This week's lucky ingredient 
is in one of them!

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:48.010
The higher the capture level, 
the more Gourmet Luck it has!

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:50.880
Alright, here we go!

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:52.250
A heaping helping...

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:55.280
Open!

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:59.290
This week's best Gourmet Luck is...

00:22:01.490 --> 00:22:02.720
...yours if you chose C!

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:05.290
No matter what you do, you may 
get a hearty dose of success!

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:08.360
If you chose A, you get this 
week's second-best luck.

00:22:08.730 --> 00:22:11.000
Make sure you're prepared before you act!

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:13.130
And, I'm sorry.

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:15.400
If you chose B, you're third.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:17.370
Be careful you don't forget anything!

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:19.670
Think things through before acting.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:23.010
Alright, finally it's Gourmet 
Good Luck Charm photo time!

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:24.710
Are you ready?

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:28.450
Toriko or one of his friends 
is going to say a few words.

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:31.080
If you take a photo of that 
scene and carry it with you

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:33.650
for a week as a good luck 
charm, you'll be even luckier!

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:35.820
Alright, here we go!

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:36.620
Three!

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:37.420
Two!

00:22:38.020 --> 00:22:38.360
One!

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:39.660
Scoop chance!

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:42.190
Don't forget to be grateful!

00:22:42.490 --> 00:22:44.060
Eat everything off your plate, yo!

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:46.060
Check it out!

00:22:46.870 --> 00:22:49.230
Uh... Our first time with 
this and it's Ponkochi...?

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:56.440
I-I think Toriko will appear starting 
next week, so don't miss it!

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:03.410
And now, what you've all been 
waiting for... Check it out!

00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:09.820
It's a natural execution grounds, where no one can trespass.

00:23:10.250 --> 00:23:13.460
Toriko takes on the impregnable water fortress.

00:23:13.980 --> 00:23:16.990
Shocking Rapids! Giant Waterfall, Death Falls!

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:18.700
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
